**Analyzing system tool execution**

I need to ensure that the public wall run for system tool commands excludes the huge initialization overhead using ordinary Popen. The initialization should ideally take about 5 seconds, plus load times, maybe? Direct trials show CPU usage around 5.5, but the wall tool takes about 2 minutes? It looks like there’s around 50 seconds of CPU time and 60 seconds of sleep. I have to test the public run limit soon to adjust the resource budget!
